{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>Faithful.</b> The wounds of a friend are strong — he wounds and crushes in the open rebuke that is fitting, until he is disciplined. And the enemy kisses him with forceful, abundant kisses, yet does not rebuke him, in order that he be caught in his transgression. The meaning of 'abundant' is 'thick.'" "Another interpretation: 'abundant' — strong, corresponding to 'faithful,' like 'their pressing upon me.'"], :book :proverbs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 27, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Proverbs -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/mishley/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:25:00.202962701Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}